commit a5083fe7146e449d80d2622ea844f1d8df14f7eb

C03: a curiosity request without a topic is a public search on a subject the product picks, told from the page found (KNOWLEDGE1505)

KNOWLEDGE1353/1355 measured that «decime una curiosidad», «contame algo» and «explicame algo interesante» invented facts or asked which topic, and the engine returns unrelated pages for the word «curiosidad»; KNOWLEDGE1473 measured that the bare name of a well-known thing returns its public page. `effect_intent.curiosity_request` reads the topicless curiosity («decime/contame/explicame una curiosidad|algo (interesante)», «estoy aburrido», «tell me a fun fact») and the live-lookup gate admits it; `curiosity_topic` picks the subject from a list of names verified against the engine's relevance rule (stable per request and hour), and the web.search query is that subject. The composer says which subject the curiosity is about and repeats what a snippet states, naming the page, never adding facts or a question. The lists are queries, not replies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


